{
  "_doc": "Feedback #106 (2026-10-21): achievements and trophies. Read by js/sim/achievements.js. An achievement counts one tally (`track`) up to `n`; `reward` is posted to you when you earn it (`gold`, or a `gift` box of `minRarity` or better at your level). `first: true` also makes it a REALM FIRST: the first character in the realm to earn it gets the trophy named in `firstTrophy` and everyone hears it. Tallies: level (highest reached), kill, killRare, killChampion, killBoss (any boss: a dungeon's, an event's), clear (a dungeon's last boss), quest (handed in), event (an event won with a share), worldboss, siege, fish, gather, craft, cook, zones (zones entered), vharlen (reached the Burning Isle), ride, death, feedback (reports sent), feedbackDone (your reports the makers marked done). Trophies (`trophies`) are kept apart: counted per kind, shown on their own shelf, given by events (world bosses and sieges: one each time you are paid a share) and by realm firsts.",
